From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - BRepTools_WireExplorer: a pcurve too short to step along ends the exploration

GetNextParamOnPC steps along a pcurve in thousandths of its range to find a point that
differs from the reference. On a pcurve whose range is a few units of the last place wide
(a face that its fillets consumed down to a point has four of them, at parameter 2.0) the step
is below the spacing of the parameter, so startPar never changes and the loop never ends.
BRepCheck_Wire reaches it through Closed2d, so BRepCheck_Analyzer never returned.

The loop now stops when a step does not move the parameter, which gives the same answer as
running out of range: the pcurve has no second point, the explorer reports the wire as not
continuing, and the analyzer reports a defect.

Found with four r = 2 fillets on a 4 x 4 face of a cube (#1568). Adds a GTest that runs the
explorer on such a wire under a deadline.

Upstream: Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1666 (fork branch SecondMouseAU/OCCT fix/wireexplorer-pcurve-step). This is the form of that
pull request as it stacks on the earlier patches of this series; where it differs from the pull request
as submitted it is only in the lines the stack made conflict (see Scripts/patches/README.md). The DRAW
test cases under tests/ that the pull request edits are not part of this patch: the build has no Draw.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BRepTools/BRepTools_WireExplorer.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BRepTools/BRepTools_WireExplorer.cxx
index 4335c1f94a..ae9b203e59 100644
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BRepTools/BRepTools_WireExplorer.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKBRep/BRepTools/BRepTools_WireExplorer.cxx
@@ -812,8 +812,14 @@ double GetNextParamOnPC(const occ::handle<Geom2d_Curve>& aPC,
     bool   nextPntOnEdge = false;
     while (!nextPntOnEdge && startPar < lP)
     {
-      gp_Pnt2d pnt;
+      gp_Pnt2d     pnt;
+      const double aPrevPar = startPar;
       startPar += dP;
+      // A step below the spacing of the parameter makes no progress.
+      if (startPar <= aPrevPar)
+      {
+        break;
+      }
       aPC->D0(startPar, pnt);
       if (std::abs(aPRef.X() - pnt.X()) < tolU && std::abs(aPRef.Y() - pnt.Y()) < tolV)
       {
@@ -843,8 +849,14 @@ double GetNextParamOnPC(const occ::handle<Geom2d_Curve>& aPC,
     bool   nextPntOnEdge = false;
     while (!nextPntOnEdge && startPar > fP)
     {
-      gp_Pnt2d pnt;
+      gp_Pnt2d     pnt;
+      const double aPrevPar = startPar;
       startPar -= dP;
+      // A step below the spacing of the parameter makes no progress.
+      if (startPar >= aPrevPar)
+      {
+        break;
+      }
       aPC->D0(startPar, pnt);
       if (std::abs(aPRef.X() - pnt.X()) < tolU && std::abs(aPRef.Y() - pnt.Y()) < tolV)
       {
